1
00:00:00,460 --> 00:00:01,070
Forty-eight per cent.

2
00:00:01,120 --> 00:00:05,530
That's roughly how much value a 2022
Tesla Model Y rear-wheel drive had lost

3
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:10,170
by early 2026, according to
Savvy, using RedBook pricing data.

4
00:00:10,220 --> 00:00:13,130
A BYD Atto 3 was down
about thirty-nine per cent.

5
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:14,450
And here's the thing.

6
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:16,110
That may only be the beginning.

7
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:17,650
Because in 2027,

8
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:20,980
a wave of electric cars is set to
hit the Australian used market.

9
00:00:21,030 --> 00:00:24,690
Cars that were bought on novated
leases when the electric car tax break

10
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:27,950
started in 2022 are now coming back.

11
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,590
Pickles, one of Australia's
biggest auction houses,

12
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:34,830
says its ex-novated lease volumes in
the September quarter of 2026 were

13
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:38,610
already 157 per cent higher
than at the start of the year.

14
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:41,030
And as Pickles' general
manager of motor vehicles,

15
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:42,370
Chris Shaw, put it:

16
00:00:42,420 --> 00:00:45,890
"The volumes coming through now are
really just the beginning." So what

17
00:00:45,940 --> 00:00:48,950
happens to used EV prices in 2027?

18
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,330
Is this a disaster for
people who own an EV,

19
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:54,430
or the best opportunity in
years for people who want one?

20
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:57,750
In this video, I'll show
you the real 2026 numbers,

21
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:00,070
why 2027 could be a turning point,

22
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:02,250
which EVs are losing value fastest,

23
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:05,150
and exactly what to check
before you buy or sell.

24
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:08,760
Because getting the timing wrong on
a used EV could cost you thousands.

25
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:12,650
First, let's understand where
this wave is coming from.

26
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:13,640
In July 2022,

27
00:01:13,690 --> 00:01:18,070
the federal government made eligible
electric cars exempt from fringe benefits

28
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:21,690
tax when they're provided through an
employer including through a novated

29
00:01:21,740 --> 00:01:22,510
lease.

30
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:24,910
That's what's called the
Electric Car Discount.

31
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:26,650
And it changed the market.

32
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:29,530
Suddenly, a lot of workers
could afford a new EV,

33
00:01:29,580 --> 00:01:32,190
paying for it out of their pre-tax salary.

34
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:35,470
Novated leases typically run
for around three to five years.

35
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:37,370
So the first big group of those cars,

36
00:01:37,420 --> 00:01:41,610
leased from mid-2022 onwards, is
now reaching the end of its term.

37
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:44,590
When a lease ends, a lot of
those cars get handed back,

38
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:46,550
sold at auction, or traded in.

39
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:50,890
And that means more used EVs, all
arriving at roughly the same time.

40
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:55,970
NRMA noted in July 2026 that the Electric
Car Discount had just reached its

41
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:57,330
fourth anniversary.

42
00:01:57,380 --> 00:02:02,090
Pickles told the NRMA it expected more
salary-packaged EVs to be remarketed

43
00:02:02,140 --> 00:02:03,910
over the following twelve months.

44
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:05,950
And by October 2026,

45
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:10,730
Pickles reported ex-novated volumes in
the September quarter were 157 per cent

46
00:02:10,780 --> 00:02:13,070
higher than in the first
quarter of the year.

47
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:14,750
To give you a sense of scale:

48
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:19,410
more than 100,000 battery electric
cars were sold new in Australia in 2025

49
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:23,750
alone, according to CarsGuide
about 8.3 per cent of the market.

50
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:25,630
By September 2026,

51
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:29,350
EVs were making up more than twenty-four
per cent of new car sales in a single

52
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:29,650
month.

53
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:33,010
Every one of those cars will
eventually become a used car.

54
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:36,210
The used EV market is only
going to get bigger from here.

55
00:02:36,260 --> 00:02:37,530
And there's another twist.

56
00:02:37,580 --> 00:02:41,690
As we covered in our last
video on 2027 EV changes,

57
00:02:41,740 --> 00:02:44,910
the Electric Car Discount
itself is being wound back.

58
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:47,050
From the 1st of April 2027,

59
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:51,910
the full exemption only applies to
new EVs costing $75,000 or less.

60
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:55,110
That could change how many people
choose to take out a new lease on an

61
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:58,460
expensive EV and how many
decide to buy used instead.

62
00:02:59,192 --> 00:03:02,402
Now, here's what makes this story more
interesting than a simple "prices are

63
00:03:02,452 --> 00:03:03,882
crashing" headline.

64
00:03:03,932 --> 00:03:07,342
2026 has actually been a
strong year for used EVs.

65
00:03:07,392 --> 00:03:08,022
Why?

66
00:03:08,072 --> 00:03:08,802
Fuel.

67
00:03:08,852 --> 00:03:11,582
When petrol and diesel prices
spiked earlier this year,

68
00:03:11,632 --> 00:03:15,102
a lot of Australians started looking
at electric cars including second-hand

69
00:03:15,152 --> 00:03:16,022
ones.

70
00:03:16,072 --> 00:03:19,802
According to the Australian Automotive
Dealer Association and AutoGrab,

71
00:03:19,852 --> 00:03:24,142
used EV sales in the first half of
2026 rose about fifty-four per cent

72
00:03:24,192 --> 00:03:27,522
compared with the year before to
more than twenty-five thousand cars.

73
00:03:27,572 --> 00:03:31,782
At the same time, total used
car sales fell 6.6 per cent.

74
00:03:31,832 --> 00:03:34,602
And used EVs started selling faster.

75
00:03:34,652 --> 00:03:38,632
The NRMA reported that the average time
to sell a used EV fell from more than

76
00:03:38,682 --> 00:03:41,882
sixty days in January to
under forty days in June.

77
00:03:41,932 --> 00:03:45,182
Pickles had its biggest quarter on
record for used EVs in the September

78
00:03:45,232 --> 00:03:48,682
quarter of 2026, with more than 440 sold,

79
00:03:48,732 --> 00:03:51,402
and more than two hundred
in September alone.

80
00:03:51,452 --> 00:03:53,182
Over the twelve months to September,

81
00:03:53,232 --> 00:03:58,162
it sold more than 1,580 used EVs
more than double the year before.

82
00:03:58,212 --> 00:04:00,562
Which brands are people
buying second-hand?

83
00:04:00,612 --> 00:04:04,302
According to the NRMA's report
on AADA and AutoGrab data,

84
00:04:04,352 --> 00:04:06,082
Tesla was by far the biggest,

85
00:04:06,132 --> 00:04:12,342
with 7,402 used sales in the first
half of 2026 up forty-eight per cent.

86
00:04:12,392 --> 00:04:16,862
MG was second by volume, with 2,582.

87
00:04:16,912 --> 00:04:21,042
Kia had 1,927 more than
double the year before.

88
00:04:21,092 --> 00:04:26,642
BYD had 1,767, up almost 175 per cent.

89
00:04:26,692 --> 00:04:30,262
And Polestar and Volkswagen
both grew from small bases,

90
00:04:30,312 --> 00:04:33,362
with Volkswagen up more
than 1,300 per cent.

91
00:04:33,412 --> 00:04:35,122
Interest exploded too.

92
00:04:35,172 --> 00:04:39,282
Pickles said its EV pages drew more
than 20,000 visitors in the June quarter

93
00:04:39,332 --> 00:04:43,182
of 2026 up from about
2,000 a year earlier.

94
00:04:43,232 --> 00:04:47,442
And carsales reported that EV searches
jumped almost seventy-seven per cent in

95
00:04:47,492 --> 00:04:52,022
a single week in March 2026,
when fuel prices were soaring.

96
00:04:52,072 --> 00:04:53,722
And it's not just city buyers.

97
00:04:53,772 --> 00:04:57,402
Pickles said regional buyers took
thirty-two per cent of its used EV purchases

98
00:04:57,452 --> 00:05:01,262
in the 2026 financial year,
up from twenty-seven per cent.

99
00:05:01,312 --> 00:05:05,832
In Queensland, almost half of its
used EV sales went to regional buyers.

100
00:05:06,645 --> 00:05:08,235
So what happened to prices?

101
00:05:08,285 --> 00:05:12,455
Pickles uses an index from Datium
Insights to track used car values.

102
00:05:12,505 --> 00:05:18,495
Its Used EV Index rose from
104 in February 2026 to 122 in

103
00:05:18,545 --> 00:05:20,955
May that was the peak of the fuel crisis.

104
00:05:21,005 --> 00:05:23,915
Then it eased back to 107 by September.

105
00:05:23,965 --> 00:05:27,095
In other words, used EV prices
jumped during the fuel spike,

106
00:05:27,145 --> 00:05:29,235
and then started coming back down.

107
00:05:29,285 --> 00:05:32,155
You can see the same pattern
in Pickles' auction prices.

108
00:05:32,205 --> 00:05:37,755
The NRMA reported the average used EV
sale price at Pickles was about $35,500

109
00:05:37,805 --> 00:05:42,415
in January, rose to
about $41,500 in April,

110
00:05:42,465 --> 00:05:48,415
then fell back to $35,500 in
May and about $31,500 in June.

111
00:05:48,465 --> 00:05:52,595
And the average odometer reading went
up from about 29,000 kilometres earlier

112
00:05:52,645 --> 00:05:56,655
in the year to about 51,000
kilometres by May and June.

113
00:05:56,705 --> 00:05:59,555
More older, higher-kilometre
EVs are coming through.

114
00:05:59,605 --> 00:06:03,395
And remember, the long-term picture
for EV depreciation has been tough.

115
00:06:03,445 --> 00:06:08,095
A 2025 analysis by Pickles and Datium
Insights found that after two years,

116
00:06:08,145 --> 00:06:11,795
a Tesla Model 3 kept about
fifty-four per cent of its value,

117
00:06:11,845 --> 00:06:13,895
a Model Y about fifty-eight per cent,

118
00:06:13,945 --> 00:06:19,255
an MG4 about fifty per cent, and a
BYD Atto 3 about fifty-four per cent.

119
00:06:19,305 --> 00:06:22,715
Compare that with a Toyota RAV4
at about eighty-eight per cent,

120
00:06:22,765 --> 00:06:27,115
a LandCruiser at about eighty-eight,
and a HiLux at about eighty-five.

121
00:06:27,165 --> 00:06:28,595
There's another way to measure this:

122
00:06:28,645 --> 00:06:31,555
how much of their value cars hold
compared with similar vehicles,

123
00:06:31,605 --> 00:06:34,015
and how often sellers
have to cut the price.

124
00:06:34,065 --> 00:06:38,415
The AADA and AutoGrab track this
for cars aged one to five years.

125
00:06:38,465 --> 00:06:39,835
In May 2026,

126
00:06:39,885 --> 00:06:43,547
they put the average residual value for
hybrids at about ninety-four per cent,

127
00:06:43,597 --> 00:06:45,575
plug-in hybrids at about
eighty-four per cent,

128
00:06:45,625 --> 00:06:48,535
and electric vehicles at
about seventy-five per cent.

129
00:06:48,585 --> 00:06:51,875
So EVs were still holding
value less well than hybrids.

130
00:06:51,925 --> 00:06:53,995
But fewer EVs needed a discount.

131
00:06:54,045 --> 00:06:57,885
The share of used EVs that had to be
discounted fell from about forty-six per

132
00:06:57,935 --> 00:07:00,755
cent in January to
forty-four per cent in May.

133
00:07:00,805 --> 00:07:03,215
For petrol cars, it was
about fifty-one per cent,

134
00:07:03,265 --> 00:07:05,695
and for diesel almost fifty-two per cent.

135
00:07:05,745 --> 00:07:07,275
So in 2026,

136
00:07:07,325 --> 00:07:11,295
used EVs actually needed fewer price
cuts than petrol and diesel cars.

137
00:07:11,345 --> 00:07:14,055
So the question for 2027 is simple.

138
00:07:14,105 --> 00:07:17,315
When thousands of ex-lease EVs
arrive, will demand keep up?

139
00:07:17,365 --> 00:07:19,165
Or will prices fall again?

140
00:07:19,949 --> 00:07:23,619
Before we get into which EVs are
most at risk, a quick favour.

141
00:07:23,669 --> 00:07:26,999
Do you own an EV or are you
thinking of buying a used one?

142
00:07:27,049 --> 00:07:30,679
Tell me in the comments what you'd pay
for a three-year-old Tesla Model 3 or

143
00:07:30,729 --> 00:07:32,259
BYD Atto 3.

144
00:07:32,309 --> 00:07:34,499
I want to see where the market really is.

145
00:07:34,549 --> 00:07:35,499
And if you want honest,

146
00:07:35,549 --> 00:07:39,679
fact-checked videos about what's
changing for Aussie drivers in 2027,

147
00:07:39,729 --> 00:07:40,539
hit subscribe.

148
00:07:40,589 --> 00:07:42,369
It's free and it really helps.

149
00:07:43,181 --> 00:07:46,991
So which used EVs are losing
value fastest and why?

150
00:07:47,041 --> 00:07:49,491
The biggest reason is new car prices.

151
00:07:49,541 --> 00:07:50,781
In April 2026,

152
00:07:50,831 --> 00:07:56,041
carsales pointed out that you can now
buy a brand-new EV for as little as

153
00:07:56,091 --> 00:08:00,651
$23,990 plus on-road costs the BYD Atto 1.

154
00:08:00,701 --> 00:08:04,071
When new cars get cheaper, used
cars have to get cheaper too.

155
00:08:04,121 --> 00:08:08,711
Carsales also said higher-priced
EVs have generally lost value first,

156
00:08:08,761 --> 00:08:13,291
and that Tesla's repeated price cuts on
the Model 3 and Model Y quickly reset

157
00:08:13,341 --> 00:08:14,551
used prices.

158
00:08:14,601 --> 00:08:15,671
Early long-range EVs,

159
00:08:15,721 --> 00:08:19,431
like the Hyundai Kona Electric
and the Tesla Model 3 Long Range,

160
00:08:19,481 --> 00:08:21,211
have lost some of their premium.

161
00:08:21,261 --> 00:08:23,451
And because buyers want
the latest versions,

162
00:08:23,501 --> 00:08:25,591
earlier models can look dated quickly.

163
00:08:25,641 --> 00:08:27,571
Let's put some real numbers on that.

164
00:08:27,621 --> 00:08:29,351
Savvy, using RedBook data,

165
00:08:29,401 --> 00:08:34,616
said in March 2026 that a 2022 Tesla
Model Y rear-wheel drive was about

166
00:08:34,666 --> 00:08:37,251
forty-eight per cent cheaper
than when it was new,

167
00:08:37,301 --> 00:08:40,651
and a BYD Atto 3 was down
about thirty-nine per cent.

168
00:08:40,701 --> 00:08:44,571
Savvy's Adrian Edlington said it "creates
real opportunities for Australians

169
00:08:44,621 --> 00:08:48,131
looking at the used EV market."
And that's the flip side.

170
00:08:48,181 --> 00:08:51,711
Every dollar an owner loses is
a dollar a used buyer saves.

171
00:08:51,761 --> 00:08:53,418
There's another factor: competition.

172
00:08:53,468 --> 00:08:59,671
Hyundai cut up to $13,857 from some
versions of the new Kona Electric in

173
00:08:59,721 --> 00:09:01,211
2026.

174
00:09:01,261 --> 00:09:04,771
Brands are under pressure from the
emissions rules to sell more EVs,

175
00:09:04,821 --> 00:09:06,811
and that often means discounting.

176
00:09:06,861 --> 00:09:10,731
Every cut on a new car puts more
pressure on the price of a used one.

177
00:09:10,781 --> 00:09:11,751
On the other hand,

178
00:09:11,801 --> 00:09:14,131
cheaper EVs and models
with fewer direct rivals,

179
00:09:14,181 --> 00:09:15,691
like the GWM Ora,

180
00:09:15,741 --> 00:09:19,661
have been less exposed to sudden
price swings, according to carsales.

181
00:09:20,479 --> 00:09:23,769
Now here's some good news for anyone
worried about buying a used EV:

182
00:09:23,819 --> 00:09:24,609
the batteries.

183
00:09:24,659 --> 00:09:28,609
The biggest fear people have with a
second-hand electric car is the battery.

184
00:09:28,659 --> 00:09:29,709
Will it be worn out?

185
00:09:29,759 --> 00:09:31,789
Will it cost a fortune to replace?

186
00:09:31,839 --> 00:09:35,809
Pickles looked at battery health data
from more than 2,500 battery electric

187
00:09:35,859 --> 00:09:36,549
vehicles.

188
00:09:36,599 --> 00:09:39,309
On average, the state of
health was ninety-six per cent.

189
00:09:39,359 --> 00:09:42,709
For vehicles over five years old,
it was ninety-three per cent.

190
00:09:42,759 --> 00:09:46,289
And even for vehicles that had
done more than 120,000 kilometres,

191
00:09:46,339 --> 00:09:47,909
it was eighty-nine per cent.

192
00:09:47,959 --> 00:09:49,959
That's a lot better
than many people expect.

193
00:09:50,009 --> 00:09:53,409
It doesn't mean every battery
is perfect charging habits,

194
00:09:53,459 --> 00:09:55,989
climate and the specific model all matter.

195
00:09:56,039 --> 00:09:59,769
But it does suggest most used EVs on
the market still have most of their

196
00:09:59,819 --> 00:10:01,069
battery capacity.

197
00:10:01,119 --> 00:10:02,289
Buyers have noticed, too.

198
00:10:02,339 --> 00:10:06,609
The average used EV sold by Pickles
in the September quarter was about 3.1

199
00:10:06,659 --> 00:10:10,869
years old, with roughly 44,000 kilometres
about fifty per cent more kilometres

200
00:10:10,919 --> 00:10:12,389
than two years earlier.

201
00:10:12,439 --> 00:10:13,729
And they're still selling.

202
00:10:13,779 --> 00:10:17,189
That suggests buyers are becoming more
comfortable with higher-kilometre EVs,

203
00:10:17,239 --> 00:10:20,529
which is exactly what the
2027 lease wave will bring.

204
00:10:20,579 --> 00:10:22,649
And there's another surprising number.

205
00:10:22,699 --> 00:10:26,629
Pickles found that statutory write-off
EVs sold for sixteen per cent more than

206
00:10:26,679 --> 00:10:28,789
comparable petrol and diesel vehicles,

207
00:10:28,839 --> 00:10:32,369
and repairable write-offs sold
for seventy-one per cent more.

208
00:10:32,419 --> 00:10:35,759
Damaged EVs are in demand, mostly
for their parts and batteries.

209
00:10:36,569 --> 00:10:38,719
So what does 2027 look like?

210
00:10:38,769 --> 00:10:43,179
Here's my honest read, based on the data
not a prediction anyone can promise.

211
00:10:43,229 --> 00:10:45,359
On one side, supply is going up.

212
00:10:45,409 --> 00:10:47,659
More ex-novated EVs are coming back.

213
00:10:47,709 --> 00:10:49,399
More brands are selling EVs.

214
00:10:49,449 --> 00:10:52,579
More EVs are reaching three,
four and five years old.

215
00:10:52,629 --> 00:10:56,279
Pickles' own manager says the current
volumes are "really just the beginning."

216
00:10:56,329 --> 00:10:58,919
On the other side,
demand is also going up.

217
00:10:58,969 --> 00:11:01,099
More Australians are considering EVs,

218
00:11:01,149 --> 00:11:04,699
regional buyers are getting involved,
and dealers are getting more confident.

219
00:11:04,749 --> 00:11:08,319
Pickles' Brendon Green said dealers
increasing their participation "tells us

220
00:11:08,369 --> 00:11:11,959
they're becoming more confident."
The AADA's James Voortman said:

221
00:11:12,009 --> 00:11:15,779
"As more EVs enter the used market
and consumers become increasingly

222
00:11:15,829 --> 00:11:17,499
comfortable with the technology,

223
00:11:17,549 --> 00:11:21,579
we would expect the used EV market to
continue to mature." And then there are

224
00:11:21,629 --> 00:11:23,899
the wildcards for 2027.

225
00:11:23,949 --> 00:11:27,819
Fuel prices if they spike
again, used EV demand will jump.

226
00:11:27,869 --> 00:11:31,299
New EV prices if they keep
falling, used values will follow.

227
00:11:31,349 --> 00:11:34,659
The fringe benefits tax
change in April 2027.

228
00:11:34,709 --> 00:11:39,819
And the planned NSW road user
charge for EVs from July 2027.

229
00:11:39,869 --> 00:11:41,779
And don't forget the condition
of the cars themselves.

230
00:11:41,829 --> 00:11:46,099
The first wave of ex-lease EVs will
mostly be three to five years old,

231
00:11:46,149 --> 00:11:47,459
with one previous owner,

232
00:11:47,509 --> 00:11:51,779
and often with full service histories
because a novated lease usually includes

233
00:11:51,829 --> 00:11:52,939
scheduled servicing.

234
00:11:52,989 --> 00:11:56,499
That's exactly the kind of car
many used buyers are looking for.

235
00:11:56,549 --> 00:11:58,139
So rather than a single crash,

236
00:11:58,189 --> 00:12:01,379
the more likely picture is a market
that keeps getting bigger and more

237
00:12:01,429 --> 00:12:02,839
competitive with older,

238
00:12:02,889 --> 00:12:06,589
more expensive and higher-kilometre
EVs under the most pressure.

239
00:12:07,371 --> 00:12:10,941
So what should you do if you own an
EV and you're thinking of selling?

240
00:12:10,991 --> 00:12:12,761
First, know your numbers.

241
00:12:12,811 --> 00:12:16,221
Check comparable listings for your
exact model, year and kilometres.

242
00:12:16,271 --> 00:12:18,501
Get a valuation or an instant offer.

243
00:12:18,551 --> 00:12:20,041
That's your starting point.

244
00:12:20,091 --> 00:12:21,541
Second, think about timing.

245
00:12:21,591 --> 00:12:25,241
Carsales suggested selling sooner may
suit owners nearing the end of their

246
00:12:25,291 --> 00:12:29,201
battery warranty, owners whose car has
been overtaken by a cheaper or updated

247
00:12:29,251 --> 00:12:32,601
model, or people who bought
early and still have equity.

248
00:12:32,651 --> 00:12:35,061
Holding may suit people who
owe more than the car is worth,

249
00:12:35,111 --> 00:12:39,441
are near the end of a lease or finance
term, or are happy with the car.

250
00:12:39,491 --> 00:12:41,181
Also, think about where you sell.

251
00:12:41,231 --> 00:12:45,181
With regional buyers now taking almost
a third of Pickles' used EV sales,

252
00:12:45,231 --> 00:12:47,881
the buyer for your car
might not be in your suburb.

253
00:12:47,931 --> 00:12:51,101
Listing nationally, or selling through
a channel that reaches regional buyers,

254
00:12:51,151 --> 00:12:52,901
could get you a better price.

255
00:12:52,951 --> 00:12:54,421
Third, prove the battery.

256
00:12:54,471 --> 00:12:57,401
A battery health report can
make a big difference to buyers.

257
00:12:57,451 --> 00:13:00,841
Keep your service history and
any software updates documented.

258
00:13:00,891 --> 00:13:03,281
And fourth, if your car is
coming off a novated lease,

259
00:13:03,331 --> 00:13:06,861
compare your residual payment
with the car's real market value.

260
00:13:06,911 --> 00:13:08,921
If the car is worth
more than the residual,

261
00:13:08,971 --> 00:13:11,361
you may be able to keep
or sell it for a profit.

262
00:13:11,411 --> 00:13:12,461
If it's worth less,

263
00:13:12,511 --> 00:13:15,531
talk to your lease provider about
your options before the end date.

264
00:13:16,255 --> 00:13:20,045
And if you're buying a used EV
in 2027, here's your checklist.

265
00:13:20,095 --> 00:13:23,425
Step one: ask for a battery health report.

266
00:13:23,475 --> 00:13:25,605
Many dealers and auction
houses can provide one,

267
00:13:25,655 --> 00:13:28,985
and some brands can generate a
report through their service centres.

268
00:13:29,035 --> 00:13:31,545
If the seller won't provide one, ask why.

269
00:13:31,595 --> 00:13:33,725
Don't just trust the
range on the dashboard.

270
00:13:33,775 --> 00:13:36,085
Step two: check the battery warranty.

271
00:13:36,135 --> 00:13:39,065
Many EV batteries have a
warranty of around eight years,

272
00:13:39,115 --> 00:13:40,885
often with a kilometre limit.

273
00:13:40,935 --> 00:13:44,085
Find out exactly how much is left,
and whether it transfers to you.

274
00:13:44,135 --> 00:13:46,315
Step three: check the charging equipment.

275
00:13:46,365 --> 00:13:48,685
Does the car come with a charging cable?

276
00:13:48,735 --> 00:13:50,305
Does it support fast charging?

277
00:13:50,355 --> 00:13:52,145
And where will you charge it at home?

278
00:13:52,195 --> 00:13:53,945
Step four: compare with new.

279
00:13:53,995 --> 00:13:58,045
With new EVs from about
$24,000 before on-road costs,

280
00:13:58,095 --> 00:14:01,605
make sure the used one is genuinely
cheaper once you add everything up

281
00:14:01,655 --> 00:14:04,705
including warranty,
servicing and running costs.

282
00:14:04,755 --> 00:14:06,905
Step five: check the model's history.

283
00:14:06,955 --> 00:14:08,185
Has it had recalls?

284
00:14:08,235 --> 00:14:11,625
Has the model been updated recently,
making the older version look dated?

285
00:14:11,675 --> 00:14:14,835
And does the brand have service
and parts support near you?

286
00:14:14,885 --> 00:14:17,725
Step six: get a pre-purchase inspection,

287
00:14:17,775 --> 00:14:20,265
ideally from a workshop that knows EVs.

288
00:14:20,315 --> 00:14:24,865
Check the tyres too EVs are heavy and
can wear tyres faster and look for any

289
00:14:24,915 --> 00:14:28,565
sign of accident damage underneath,
especially near the battery.

290
00:14:28,615 --> 00:14:30,765
Step seven: if you're in New South Wales,

291
00:14:30,815 --> 00:14:35,165
factor in the planned road user charge
from July 2027 roughly a few hundred

292
00:14:35,215 --> 00:14:38,775
dollars a year for an average
driver, based on the proposed rate.

293
00:14:39,517 --> 00:14:43,507
So, could used EV prices
crash in Australia in 2027?

294
00:14:43,557 --> 00:14:44,417
Here's the honest answer.

295
00:14:44,467 --> 00:14:46,407
The supply wave is real.

296
00:14:46,457 --> 00:14:48,427
Ex-novated lease volumes are rising fast,

297
00:14:48,477 --> 00:14:51,787
and they're likely to
keep rising into 2027.

298
00:14:51,837 --> 00:14:54,847
Older and more expensive EVs
have already lost a lot of value.

299
00:14:54,897 --> 00:14:58,947
And every new-car price cut
pushes used prices down further.

300
00:14:58,997 --> 00:15:00,687
Let's recap the key numbers.

301
00:15:00,737 --> 00:15:05,247
Used EV sales up about fifty-four
per cent in the first half of 2026.

302
00:15:05,297 --> 00:15:09,747
Pickles' ex-novated lease volumes up
157 per cent in the September quarter

303
00:15:09,797 --> 00:15:11,277
compared with the March quarter.

304
00:15:11,327 --> 00:15:16,567
The Used EV Index up from 104
to 122 during the fuel spike,

305
00:15:16,617 --> 00:15:19,087
then back to 107 by September.

306
00:15:19,137 --> 00:15:23,147
Average battery health of ninety-six
per cent across more than 2,500 EVs.

307
00:15:23,197 --> 00:15:26,917
And a new EV now starting from under
twenty-four thousand dollars before

308
00:15:26,967 --> 00:15:28,287
on-road costs.

309
00:15:28,337 --> 00:15:29,987
But demand has grown too.

310
00:15:30,037 --> 00:15:32,687
Used EV sales jumped in 2026,

311
00:15:32,737 --> 00:15:34,087
regional buyers are joining in,

312
00:15:34,137 --> 00:15:36,707
and battery health data is
better than many people fear.

313
00:15:36,757 --> 00:15:38,967
So instead of one big crash,

314
00:15:39,017 --> 00:15:40,907
the more likely outcome is a bigger,

315
00:15:40,957 --> 00:15:44,787
more competitive used EV market where
buyers have more choice and better

316
00:15:44,837 --> 00:15:47,867
prices, and sellers need
to be smarter about timing.

317
00:15:47,917 --> 00:15:50,767
And whatever you do, don't
rely on old assumptions.

318
00:15:50,817 --> 00:15:55,167
The used EV market in 2026 has moved
fast up during the fuel crisis,

319
00:15:55,217 --> 00:15:56,807
and back down since.

320
00:15:56,857 --> 00:15:59,487
It could move just as fast in 2027.

321
00:15:59,537 --> 00:16:03,027
Check real listings and real
auction results, not headlines.

322
00:16:03,077 --> 00:16:03,867
If you're buying,

323
00:16:03,917 --> 00:16:07,947
2027 could be one of the best
years ever to pick up a used EV.

324
00:16:07,997 --> 00:16:08,807
If you're selling,

325
00:16:08,857 --> 00:16:11,847
know your numbers and don't wait
too long if your car is about to be

326
00:16:11,897 --> 00:16:12,667
overtaken.

327
00:16:12,717 --> 00:16:14,247
If this helped, hit like,

328
00:16:14,297 --> 00:16:17,807
subscribe and share it with someone
who's thinking about a used EV.

329
00:16:17,857 --> 00:16:22,107
Tell me in the comments: would you buy
a second-hand electric car in 2027?

